{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_kill_switch_plan_overview", "label": "Exfiltration Guard Implementation Plan", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/KILL_SWITCH_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chose an application-level policy engine over a network-level sandbox (custom Docker networking / iptables egress allowlisting) because it is pure Node.js, needs no changes to container capabilities, and behaves identically across Docker, Colima, and rootless Podman \u2014 the three engines the Starter Kit must support. The residual risk that a single command can start executing before it is observed and reacted to is documented explicitly rather than hidden, as the acceptance checklist requires."}, {"id": "docs_kill_switch_plan_threat_model_section", "label": "Kill Switch Plan Threat Model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/KILL_SWITCH_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_kill_switch_plan_policy_decision_type", "label": "PolicyDecision Type", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/KILL_SWITCH_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_kill_switch_plan_command_policy_module", "label": "command-policy.ts Design", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/KILL_SWITCH_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "evaluateCommand is a pure, I/O-free function over an ordered deny-rule table with no container knowledge, deliberately isolated so it is unit-testable with a table of allow/deny command strings \u2014 the core 'backend policy decision' the rubric wants to see tested in isolation."}, {"id": "docs_kill_switch_plan_demo_script", "label": "Kill Switch Demo Script", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/KILL_SWITCH_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_kill_switch_plan_canary_secret", "label": "Canary Secret Seeding", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/KILL_SWITCH_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_kill_switch_plan_event_timing", "label": "item.started vs item.completed Timing Confirmation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/KILL_SWITCH_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Whether the engine achieves prevention or only fast containment depends on whether Codex's item.started carries the command before it finishes executing. The implementation checks the policy at whichever event first reveals the command text, so it automatically gets the best available timing without a redesign once confirmed; claims in the README/demo were deliberately scoped to 'terminated immediately, blocking continuation' rather than 'zero bytes ever reach the destination' until this was verified live."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_kill_switch_plan_overview", "target": "docs_hackathon_extension_guide_kill_switch", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/KILL_SWITCH_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_kill_switch_plan_overview", "target": "readme_limitations", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/KILL_SWITCH_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_kill_switch_plan_overview", "target": "docs_policy_evaluation_defect_quote_wrapping", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/KILL_SWITCH_PLAN.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_kill_switch_plan_